# --- s039 Book I d.10 q.un. = Ord. I d.10 q.un.
n("n655","s039-01","Circa decimam distinctionem","la","source","= Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 10 q. un., *utrum Spiritus Sanctus producatur per modum voluntatis* (Vat. IV). Lombard, *Sent.* I d. 10 (the Holy Spirit as the love of Father and Son).","to-verify")
n("n656","s039-01","Augustinus. 15. de trinitate","la","source","Augustine, *De Trin.* XV (the Holy Spirit as love and gift, XV 17.27–19.37). The verbatim words *procedit necessario* are not located; they may be the scholastic gloss of the objection as Scotus states it.","to-verify")
n("n657","s039-02","doctoris solennis in summa articulo. 60. q. 1.","la","source","Henry of Ghent (*doctor solemnis*), *Summa quaestionum ordinariarum* a. 60 q. 1, on the distinction of nature and will as principles of emanation.","to-verify")
n("n658","s039-02","quodlibeto. 6. q. 1.","la","source","Henry of Ghent, *Quodl.* VI q. 1 (notional acts founded on essential acts). Scotus's reply is in *Ord.* I d. 10.","to-verify")
n("n659","s039-02","quodlibeto. 5. questione. 1.","la","source","Henry of Ghent, *Quodl.* V q. 1 (on the distinction of attributes in God, here of will and nature, *secundum rationem*).","to-verify")
n("n660","s039-04","sine","la","textual","A reads *sine actu*, which contradicts the argument. B reads *in actu intellectus et voluntatis* (B also writes *ethi.*). Read *in* with B.","verified")
n("n661","s039-04","10. ethicorum","la","source","Aristotle, *EN* X 7–8, 1177a12–1178b32 (happiness as the activity of the highest part). The ascription of beatitude to intellect *and* will is scholastic, not Aristotle's.","certain")
n("n662","s039-04","Sanctus doctor prima parte. q. 19. articulo. 1.","la","source","Thomas Aquinas, *ST* I q. 19 a. 1 (*utrum in Deo sit voluntas*): *voluntas intellectum consequitur*; the parallel with sensitive appetite is in the corpus. Gorris calls Thomas *sanctus doctor* (canonised 1323).","certain")
n("n663","s039-04","Augustino. 5. de trinitate. c. 17.","la","source","Augustine, *De Trin.* V 14.15: *exiit enim non quomodo natus, sed quomodo datus*. Gorris's chapter number 17 follows a different capitulation.","to-verify")
n("n664","s039-05","reducuntur ad aliquod vnum","la","source","Scotus's argument from the reduction of productive principles to the two irreducible ones, nature and will (*Ord.* I d. 10 q. un.; cf. *Quaest. in Metaph.* IX q. 15 on the division of active powers into nature and will).","to-verify")
n("n665","s039-06","quatuor conclusiones","la","source","On essence and will as one total principle of spiration (essence concurring as object, will as power), cf. Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 10 and the parallel for the intellect and the Word, *Ord.* I d. 2 p. 2 qq. 1–4.","to-verify")
n("n666","s039-07","non est de intentione scoti","la","historical","A school dispute on Scotus's intention: some held that Scotus posits no begotten act of understanding or willing in God (the acts are *innati*, not *eliciti*). Here Scotus is named in the text. The holders of this view are not identified.","uncertain")
n("n667","s039-07","illicitos","la","textual","*illicitos* A and B: = *elicitos* (i/e and ll spelling), not *illicitus* ‘unlawful’. B reads *illicitos .s. innatos* (‘elicited, that is, innate’?) for A's *illicitos sed innatos*. A gives the better sense.","verified")
n("n668","s039-09","secundum Henricum","la","source","Henry of Ghent's fourfold sense of *natura*: *Summa* a. 54 q. 3 / a. 60; cf. *Quodl.* VI q. 1. Exact locus to be checked.","to-verify")
n("n669","s039-09","est enim infinitas proprius modus","la","source","Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 10 q. un.: the divine will is a principle of communicating the nature *ut infinita*; infinity as an intrinsic mode (cf. *Ord.* I d. 8 p. 1 q. 3).","to-verify")
n("n670","s039-11","Doctor dicit quod ibi est libertas et necessitas","la","source","Scotus, *Ord.* I d. 10 q. un. (the necessity of spiration stands with freedom; freedom has its own necessity, as nature has its own contingency). Cf. *Quodl.* q. 16.","to-verify")
n("n671","s039-11","quidam doctor","la","historical","Unnamed. The distinction between necessity *quoad actum* and freedom *quoad electionem*, and the *libertas complacentiae*, are characteristic of later Scotist discussion, but the author is not identified.","uncertain")
n("n672","s039-04","⟨in⟩","en","translation","Translating B's *in actu*, not A's *sine*.")
n("n673","s039-07","elicited","en","translation","*illicitos* = *elicitos*.")
n("n674","s039-11","freedom of complacency","en","translation","*libertas complacentiae*: the freedom of the will's delight or consent in a good that is necessarily loved.")

# --- B collation (full): B55L–B57R
upd("n656", append=" B reads *Aug. xiij. de tri.* here, but *Aug. 15. de tri.* (*xv*) in §s039-08.")
n("n974","s039-02","dum tertio respondet dubio","la","textual","B: *Tunc tercio respondet dubio*.","certain")
n("n975","s039-07","ponere noticiam genitam","la","textual","B: *pure noticiam genitam*, presumably a misreading of *ponere*.","certain")
n("n976","s039-08","est sine imperfectione","la","textual","B: *est sua perfectione*. A's *sine imperfectione* is the Scotist formula and is kept.","certain")
